{{-- The WordPress admin theme's list screen (`wp-admin/edit.php`): Ignite's list page values (the same as its `index` view reads) in WordPress's markup. The heading with "Add New" as `.page-title-action`, the status tabs as WordPress's status links (`.subsubsub`), the search box, and the `.wp-list-table.widefat.fixed.striped` table: its heading row (`.manage-column`), its striped rows, and each row's actions in `.row-actions`, which the layout's script moves under the title (WordPress's `column-primary`); without the script they stay in their own column. The pager is WordPress's `.tablenav-pages`. The markup Mission Control reads on the Media screen stays as Ignite's: the list in `<section class="ig-card p-0">`, the rows as `<tr>` with plain `<td>` cells, and the pager a `div` starting `<div class="mt-5`, without nested ones. --}}@extends('ignite::layouts.app')

